<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Local manifest: bring back the ckati sources (platform/build/kati).

  Why a local manifest at all:
    Android 11+ AOSP (and lineage-19.1) ship ckati ONLY as a prebuilt
    (prebuilts/build-tools); no release manifest carries the kati repo
    anymore. `path="build/kati"` + `name="platform/build/kati"` is the
    classic Android 9/10 manifest entry, restored here.

  Why an explicit revision (a SHA):
    The `aosp` remote's default revision is refs/tags/android-12.1.0_r22,
    which does not exist in build/kati (kati was dropped from release
    manifests, so the repo has no android-12 release tags). Syncing with
    only remote="aosp" would fail outright.

  Why this SHA (9f48932c90ca, 2021-10-20, "Merge pull request #239"):
    The prebuilt ckati carries kGitVersion="unknown" (built via soong,
    not Makefile.ckati), so the compile-time commit is not recoverable.
    Feature-string dating of the binary brackets its source to
    2021-02-23 (.KATI_ALLOW_RULES present) .. 2021-10-25 (.SHELLSTATUS
    absent). This commit is the last main-branch anchor before
    .SHELLSTATUS, i.e. the newest source still consistent with the
    prebuilt binary.

  Why a separate remote (USTC instead of the default TUNA "aosp"):
    TUNA rejects short-SHA fetches and queues full-SHA fetches behind a
    600+ position slow queue; USTC serves full-SHA shallow fetches
    directly. Only build/kati uses this remote; everything else stays on
    TUNA.

  Any source tweaks inside build/kati are managed with patchman and land
  under patchdb/code/build/kati/ (see docs/patchman.md).

  This local manifest itself lives in the repo tree at
  .repo/local_manifests/kati.xml (it is the true source, applied/refreshed
  by bootstrap.sh from the patchman copy entry under
  patchdb/code/.repo/local_manifests/kati.xml); sync_deps then fetches
  build/kati.
-->
<manifest>
  <remote name="ustc-aosp"
          fetch="https://mirrors.ustc.edu.cn/aosp/"
          review="android-review.googlesource.com" />

  <project path="build/kati"
           name="platform/build/kati"
           remote="ustc-aosp"
           revision="9f48932c90ca93bc1777561cc22d1a2587bc0333"
           groups="pdk,tradefed"
           clone-depth="1" />
</manifest>
